{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SECOND OCCURRENCE — same test, same cell, different run. Strengthens the reproduction evidence materially.\n\nRun 31737094701 (change 1731, patchset 2, after a recheck of run 31734135055 on the IDENTICAL tree):\n- macos-latest/py3.13 only; the three ubuntu cells passed both times.\n- 1 failed, 12849 passed, 65 skipped, in 1602.64s (first occurrence: 1664.64s).\n- Same test: tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render_hardening.py::test_rendered_output_is_byte_identical_to_the_landed_renderer.\n\nNEW TIMING DETAIL, which I think is the most useful thing here for reproduction: the two log events are 14 minutes apart.\n  19:57:28  .....[gw1] node down: Not properly terminated\n  20:11:28  worker 'gw1' crashed while running <the test>\nThe worker is declared down at 19:57:28 and the crash is only attributed at 20:11:28. That gap is consistent with a HANG followed by a kill, not with a fast crash — which fits the 300s-per-test-timeout hypothesis in the ticket body, but note 14 minutes is far longer than 300s, so if the per-test timeout were firing cleanly the gap should be ~5 minutes. Either the timeout is not firing on this path (pandoc subprocess not interruptible?) or the kill comes from somewhere else. Worth checking before assuming the timeout budget is the whole story.\n\nDeterminism evidence: two consecutive runs of the same patchset, same cell, same test — this is reproducible on the macOS lane, not a rare one-off. The contrast case remains change 1734, which contains 1731's exact commit plus one more and passed macos-latest/py3.13 both times.\n\nNo third recheck was attempted; 1731 is parked behind this bug's class fix."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786652175008917001,"uuid":"6da15436-97de-4dec-a707-95d1251fbd71"}